  "limitations": [
    "The 88-case survey is a feature sample, not a compatibility percentage.",
    "UNIQUE support here is for single-column ascending BINARY keys with the default ABORT constraint policy. Compound keys, other declaration policies and collations remain incomplete.",
    "Schema SELECT reads actual physical catalog records and preserves connection state, but pending transactional schema changes and nested source discovery remain limited.",
    "The single-Core-command CREATE TABLE translation theorem now explicitly excludes UNIQUE declarations, which require index creation as well. The old unrestricted theorem no longer described the live implementation.",
    "Valid empty-schema SQLite files with header text encoding 0 were discovered to be rejected; this separate gap remains open. Invalid empty-fixture baselines are not used as evidence of UNIQUE failures.",
    "The retained-catalog rollback route is still limited to ordinary unreserved 4096-byte geometry and its component catalog decoder. Broader ALTER/automatic-index renaming, large catalogs, other SQL and file/WAL semantics require further work.",
    "SIGKILL timing samples do not cover every syscall boundary or power-loss scenario. OS syscalls and executable composition remain documented trusted boundaries."
  ],
